# CODEOWNERS
#
# Maps repository paths to responsible GitHub teams/users.
# All listed owners must approve PRs that touch their paths.
#
# Ownership tiers:
#   Core     — 2 maintainer approvals + security review required
#   Domain   — 1 maintainer approval required
#   Support  — 1 review from any maintainer
#
# Review routing:
#   PRs touching ONLY support-owned paths can be auto-merged after 1 approval.
#   PRs touching ANY core-owned path require 2 approvals and security review.
#   PRs touching multiple domains require 1 approval from each domain owner.
#
# See docs/CONTRACT_DEPENDENCY_GRAPH.md for the full dependency model.
# See docs/COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX.md for version compatibility requirements.

# ── Core shared infrastructure (CRITICAL — 2 approvals + security review) ─────
# These contracts have the highest blast radius. Any change requires 2
# maintainer approvals and a security review before merging.
# SECURITY: Changes here affect ALL tenants and downstream contracts.
contracts/common_error/       @Stellar-Uzima/maintainers
contracts/common_auth/        @Stellar-Uzima/maintainers
